  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 19. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 解明 — 分からなかったことを調べて明らかにすること。\n2. 海流 — 海の中にある大きな水の流れ。\n3. 改良 — 今あるものをよりよくすること。\n4. 回路 — 電気などが通る道筋。\n5. 回廊 — 建物や中庭を囲むようにつながる廊下。\n6. カウンセラー — 悩みを聞いていっしょに考える専門の人。\n7. カウンター — 店などで客と店員が向かい合う細長い台。\n8. カウント — 数を数えること。\n9. 帰り道 — 出掛けた先から戻るときに通る道。\n10. 顔合わせ — いっしょに活動する人などが初めて集まること。\n11. 顔色 — 顔の色や表情に表れる様子。\n12. 家屋 — 人が住むためなどに建てた家。\n13. 顔立ち — 目や鼻などの形や配置による顔の様子。\n14. 顔なじみ — 何度も顔を合わせて知っている人。\n15. 顔ぶれ — 集まりなどに参加する人の取り合わせ。\n16. 顔見知り — 顔を見たことがあり互いに知っている人。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
